2-TEK Thunder Container Engine — Standalone Single-Process Server
Rule Conformance: Rule 69 (Target), Rule 29 (EOF), Rule 72 (Dynamic Paths)
Runs as a standalone single process with zero heavy multi-process dependencies.
Provides Thunder Control Dashboard UI and REST APIs:
  - GET  /                           -> Visual Thunder Control Dashboard
  - GET  /health                     -> Health & single-process PID status
  - GET  /api/v1/health              -> Health JSON
  - GET  /api/v1/thunder/status      -> Thunder microkernel & engine status
  - GET  /api/v1/thunder/containers  -> Active container instances
  - POST /api/v1/thunder/containers/run  -> Run/spawn container instance
  - POST /api/v1/thunder/containers/stop -> Stop container instance
  - GET  /api/v1/thunder/images      -> OCI image store inventory
  - GET  /api/v1/thunder/stats       -> Aggregate CPU, Memory, RPS metrics
"""

